<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jai Singh Prabhakar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1882–1937</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Jai Singh of Alwar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jai Singh Prabhakar was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of Alwar in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputana">Rajputana</a> from 1892. Gifted and well educated, he became notorious for erratic and cruel rule. After a Meo peasant uprising and misgovernment the British forced him to leave the state in 1933, and he died in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> in 1937.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jai-singh-prabhakar.jpg" alt="Jai Singh Prabhakar" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tpsn98290 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maharaja_Jai_Singh_of_Alwar_State.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
